  "note": "the family band DEFINITION stays F0 vs F1; the single-axis bands are DIAGNOSTICS that answer \"how sensitive is a post-route WNS to one physical axis\", and they change no published verdict by themselves -- this tool only asks whether the published verdicts would SURVIVE them",
  "boundary": "PROBE level, NOT paper evidence.  A single-axis band can only be measured on the circuits where that axis is active, so the single-axis bands and the two-axis band are NOT measured on the same circuits; the common-subset rows are the like-for-like comparison and they cover only 2 circuits.  The post-route WNS is quantised to 0.01 ns.  Parasitics come from estimate_parasitics, not signoff RCX."
